@startuml Dashboard Participant Diagram
title Figure X: Dashboard Optimization Participant Diagram

' Professional Sequence Diagram Styling
skinparam actorStyle awesome
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam handwritten false
skinparam monochrome false
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam roundcorner 10
skinparam ParticipantPadding 40
skinparam BoxPadding 10

skinparam sequence {
    ArrowColor #0078d4
    LifeLineBorderColor #0078d4
    LifeLineBackgroundColor #f0f7ff
    
    ParticipantBackgroundColor #f0f7ff
    ParticipantBorderColor #0078d4
    ParticipantFontSize 14
    ParticipantFontColor #0078d4
    
    ActorBackgroundColor #f0f7ff
    ActorBorderColor #0078d4
}

skinparam note {
    BackgroundColor #fff9e6
    BorderColor #d4a017
    FontSize 11
}

actor "Plant Operator" as User
participant "Dashboard UI" as UI <<Boundary>>
participant "ChillerOptimizer" as Optimizer <<Control>>
participant "Weather API" as Weather <<External Service>>
participant "ML Model API" as ML <<External Service>>
database "Supabase" as DB <<Database>>

' Interaction Flow
autonumber

User -> UI : Adjust Inputs & Run Optimization
activate UI

opt Auto-sync Wet Bulb
    UI -> Weather : Get Live Weather Data
    activate Weather
    Weather --> UI : temperature, humidity, wetBulb
    deactivate Weather
end

UI -> Optimizer : calculateSavings(load, weather, settings)
activate Optimizer

loop for each scenario
    Optimizer -> ML : POST features for Prediction
    activate ML
    ML --> Optimizer : power/efficiency result
    deactivate ML
end

Optimizer --> UI : Best result & Recommendations
deactivate Optimizer

UI -> DB : saveOptimizationHistory(entry)
activate DB
DB --> UI : Success Acknowledgment
deactivate DB

UI --> User : Display Recommendations & Metrics
deactivate UI

note right of Optimizer
  **Optimization Logic:**
  The system iterates through
  various staging and setpoint
  combinations to find the 
  minimum kW/ton.
end note

@enduml
